The rest of the backbone is in place and correctly arranged: provenance banner first and full-width above the identity bar, one row of two columns below it with no full-width pane and no page scrollbar, Code beside a tabbed Call Trace / Event Log region with Values as a separate pane under it, and the Transaction pane as a third column. No spinner, no empty pane, no prose band under the banner. But the tick scrubber is suppressed below 1780px, so at 1440 nothing expresses extent — that is finding 1, P1, and it caps the rating at 4.

The two-column split is sound and Code keeps a usable measure. The vertical budget is where it loses. The banner takes the top 20% of the viewport for a four-sentence notice on a ~600px measure in a 1440px band; Code spends four stacked header rows before its first line; the Call Trace region holds ~140px of dead space below its last frame while the Values pane beneath it is bisected by the viewport edge; and the pane column has no bottom gutter where the other three edges have 8px. The bar does not wrap here — it is one row with a single 280px void.

Highest-priority fixes: restore the bottom gutter, and move height from the Call Trace region to Values.

